<statement>
<p>
Solve the following linear system.  If the system has an infinite number of solutions, parameterize the solution set in terms of the free variables of the original system.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left\lbrace\begin{array}{ccccccccccc} {7}{x}\amp-\amp{56}{y}\amp-\amp{9}{z}\amp-\amp{2}{w}\amp-\amp{39}{v}\amp=\amp-{66}\\{5}{x}\amp-\amp{40}{y}\amp-\amp{2}{z}\amp-\amp{28}{w}\amp-\amp{19}{v}\amp=\amp-{25}\\{7}{x}\amp-\amp{56}{y}\amp-\amp{5}{z}\amp-\amp{26}{w}\amp-\amp{31}{v}\amp=\amp-{46}\end{array}\right.}</m></p>
<p>
x = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
y = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
z = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
w = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
v = <fillin characters="20"/>  

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle-{3}+{8}{y}+{8}{w}+{3}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{y}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{5}+{6}{w}-{2}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{v}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

